        "original_id": "c7dbdbe6-d839-518a-9a57-62c6c7ea3549",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Georgia, Penn State\n- Teams: 1982 Georgia Bulldogs football team\n- People: Vince Dooley\n- Events: 1982 NCAA Division I-A football season, Sugar Bowl\n- Roles: Head football coach, athletic director\n\nFacts:\n- Vince Dooley was born on September 4, 1932.\n- Vince Dooley served as head football coach at the University of Georgia from 1964 through 1988.\n- Vince Dooley served as athletic director at the University of Georgia from 1979 to 2004.\n- The 1982 Georgia Bulldogs football team represented the University of Georgia during the 1982 NCAA Division I-A football season.\n- The 1982 Georgia Bulldogs football team was led by head coach Vince Dooley.\n- In the Sugar Bowl, the top-ranked 1982 Georgia Bulldogs football team lost 23-27 to number two Penn State.",
